WEBVTT

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:09.301
It's summer!

00:00:09.301 --> 00:00:12.137
First time at the pool this year!

00:00:12.137 --> 00:00:14.181
Let's work hard!

00:00:14.181 --> 00:00:16.475
Let's make the pool clean and shiny together!

00:00:17.184 --> 00:00:18.352
Okay!

00:00:18.936 --> 00:00:20.395
Here we go!

00:00:25.776 --> 00:00:30.489
If I'm at the pool, I want to
gaze upon some girls in swimsuits.

00:00:30.489 --> 00:00:33.617
Takamine, move your hands, not your mouth!

00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:35.994
"Kyushu Ramen Saburo"

00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:37.788
"Ramen Extravagant Eating Investigation!!"

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:45.254
I like ramen, but I'm full.

00:00:46.505 --> 00:00:48.799
I'll take your slice of pork, then!

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.095
Kanasuke, you can still eat?

00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:55.013
Meat goes in a different stomach!

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:59.977
All things considered,
we're pretty popular, huh?

00:00:59.977 --> 00:01:02.229
I'm worn out every day.

00:01:02.229 --> 00:01:05.023
It's thanks to passing out those flyers.

00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:09.611
I want to erase that memory...

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:12.990
That made the Library Club really well-known.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.158
But all we've been doing are odd jobs.

00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:18.078
You're not supposed to say that.

00:01:19.663 --> 00:01:22.082
Well, time for our next job!

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.960
Let's think of this as
light exercise after a meal!

00:01:25.669 --> 00:01:27.754
We're not done...?

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.393
<i>Writing down my aspirations</i>

00:01:41.393 --> 00:01:44.146
<i>For the day when they will come true</i>

00:01:44.146 --> 00:01:49.484
<i>The time has come when</i>
<i>I want to turn to the page I marked</i>

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:54.948
<i>Although there are things I lose</i>
<i>sight of with everything that happens</i>

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.325
<i>Hey, it's all right</i>

00:01:56.325 --> 00:02:00.245
<i>The start I'm embarking on is unexpected</i>

00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:03.081
<i>The memory that you couldn't erase</i>

00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:05.751
<i>Even that sad memory</i>

00:02:05.751 --> 00:02:09.796
<i>I'll give it a different, happier reading</i>

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:15.427
<i>I feel like just that will change everything</i>

00:02:15.427 --> 00:02:16.553
<i>All Right</i>

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:19.765
<i>So come now, the way you are!</i>

00:02:19.765 --> 00:02:22.601
<i>Don't hide your weak self</i>

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:23.602
<i>On my Sheep </i>

00:02:23.602 --> 00:02:27.272
<i>Let's meet riding on a dream</i>

00:02:27.272 --> 00:02:33.237
<i>Even just calling your name as</i>
<i>I write in this book of adventures</i>

00:02:33.237 --> 00:02:36.031
<i>I'm not lost anymore</i>

00:02:36.031 --> 00:02:39.743
<i>Let's start our journey together</i>

00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:47.501
<i>Yes... more of you and me!</i>

00:02:57.344 --> 00:03:01.557
"Episode 5: The Truth Behind the Messages"

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.154
"To: The Shepherd"
"What do I have to do to meet you?"

00:03:16.154 --> 00:03:18.740
I didn't think I'd get a reply...

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:21.827
I wonder if the Shepherd is close by?

00:03:35.924 --> 00:03:37.509
I'm from the Stone Wall Research Committee.

00:03:37.509 --> 00:03:38.260
What should we do to tell people

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:39.261
"Unshaped stones"
What should we do to tell people

00:03:39.261 --> 00:03:40.637
"Stones in turtle-shell pattern"
how great stone walls are?

00:03:41.138 --> 00:03:45.851
Please tell me how I can
get back with my ex-girlfriend!

00:03:45.851 --> 00:03:49.813
I have, like, an interview
for a part-time job tomorrow,

00:03:49.813 --> 00:03:51.899
but I'm, like, nervous.

00:03:51.899 --> 00:03:55.569
I want you to teach me a
charm so I won't be nervous!

00:03:56.612 --> 00:03:59.907
This school is full of people with problems.

00:03:59.907 --> 00:04:03.076
They're all like little lost lambs, huh?

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:04.661
Yeah!

00:04:06.288 --> 00:04:08.415
Hey, will you do something about this?

00:04:08.415 --> 00:04:11.168
I'm getting a flood of complaints!

00:04:13.378 --> 00:04:14.463
Who's that?

00:04:14.463 --> 00:04:15.839
Dunno...

00:04:15.839 --> 00:04:17.216
Um...

00:04:17.216 --> 00:04:18.634
Hm?

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:23.764
Huh? Why are you all playing dumb?
It's Kodachi, the library worker.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.267
Uh, right...

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.727
Now that you mention it...

00:04:28.727 --> 00:04:32.481
How mean! Didn't we
bathe together, Cutting Board?

00:04:32.481 --> 00:04:35.067
I'm not <i>that </i>flat!

00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:35.275
I just have small, refined breasts.

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:39.071
"Refined breasts"
I just have small, refined breasts.

00:04:39.071 --> 00:04:40.656
Oh, it's Kodachi!

00:04:40.656 --> 00:04:43.784
Speaking of which,
doesn't she live next door to Kakei?

00:04:43.784 --> 00:04:47.913
More importantly, the head
library worker wants to talk to you.

00:04:47.913 --> 00:04:50.874
She said she wants you out of this room soon.

00:04:50.874 --> 00:04:52.835
What?

00:04:53.627 --> 00:04:57.339
Some circumstances of your recent use
of the clubroom have been unpardonable.

00:04:57.339 --> 00:05:03.762
Therefore, I will have you move to a location
more suitable for your present activities.

00:05:03.762 --> 00:05:06.765
We're sorry. We will try to remedy this.

00:05:09.393 --> 00:05:14.189
Yes, so please let us stay here! Please!

00:05:15.023 --> 00:05:20.362
We'll do whatever we can,
so will you please give us another chance?

00:05:21.196 --> 00:05:24.825
Then, why don't we set a grace period?

00:05:26.368 --> 00:05:29.663
Ah, this is hard work.

00:05:29.663 --> 00:05:33.250
But if we clean this place up,
I'm sure our points will go up in an instant!

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:36.461
And the library workers'
impression of us will go up, too.

00:05:36.461 --> 00:05:39.923
Let's work hard to protect our room!

00:05:39.923 --> 00:05:41.008
Yes!

00:05:41.008 --> 00:05:43.218
You seem busy every day.

00:05:46.388 --> 00:05:48.348
Mochizuki?

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:51.393
I heard about the situation
from the head library worker.

00:05:51.393 --> 00:05:55.147
It's kind of refreshing
to see you outside, Kakei.

00:05:55.147 --> 00:05:58.817
The sun is so bright I feel like
I'm going to dry up even now, though.

00:05:58.817 --> 00:06:03.488
But if it will protect our clubroom, it's no
time to be worrying about getting sunburned.

00:06:04.489 --> 00:06:06.867
You've changed...

00:06:06.867 --> 00:06:09.536
Is it the influence of the
other Library Club members?

00:06:10.579 --> 00:06:12.206
You think so?

00:06:12.206 --> 00:06:15.626
I can't really tell myself, though.

00:06:15.626 --> 00:06:21.882
Kakei, won't you join the student council
and discover a different side of yourself?

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.845
Just a little more, and I'll be able to see
something completely different, though.

00:06:26.845 --> 00:06:29.097
What? S-Stop...

00:06:29.097 --> 00:06:30.557
Just kidding.

00:06:30.557 --> 00:06:33.435
Jeez, you're so mean, Kakei.

00:06:33.435 --> 00:06:35.229
Sorry.

00:06:35.229 --> 00:06:37.606
From now on,

00:06:37.606 --> 00:06:40.025
"Library Club: Planned Policies and Club Room Use"
interviews will be handled through email reservations.

00:06:40.067 --> 00:06:43.362
They will be limited to 30 minutes per person,

00:06:43.362 --> 00:06:47.241
and we will have them come to
the club room at the appointed time.

00:06:48.075 --> 00:06:49.952
Oh, I'm so tired.

00:06:49.952 --> 00:06:51.411
Good work today!

00:06:51.411 --> 00:06:53.330
Goodbye!

00:06:55.332 --> 00:06:57.543
Tamamo, you're not going home yet?

00:06:57.543 --> 00:07:00.254
I just have a little left,
so you should go home first.

00:07:00.254 --> 00:07:01.547
Want me to help?

00:07:01.547 --> 00:07:06.176
No, there's not that much. See you tomorrow.

00:07:06.969 --> 00:07:09.471
I wonder if Sakuraba is all right...

00:07:11.223 --> 00:07:15.143
She's been doing of all the
administrative work by herself, right?

00:07:15.143 --> 00:07:17.896
On top of that, she took
care of this incident, too.

00:07:17.896 --> 00:07:20.858
She must be pretty worn out.

00:07:20.858 --> 00:07:23.193
She's not the type to complain, though.

00:07:23.193 --> 00:07:25.571
That's true, but...

00:07:25.571 --> 00:07:29.449
It's not good to have
one person bear all the burden.

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:32.244
You really like our club, don't you?

00:07:34.037 --> 00:07:35.289
What is it?

00:07:35.289 --> 00:07:40.502
Nothing, it's just that I'm surprised you
used "our" to talk about the Library Club.

00:07:46.466 --> 00:07:52.389
<i>I'm </i>the one most suitable
to be the Shepherd, not him.

00:07:52.764 --> 00:07:59.271
"Shiomi Academy
⬅ School Store #3"

00:08:07.279 --> 00:08:08.780
"Shiomi Academy General Library"

00:08:09.615 --> 00:08:13.744
It's not good to have
one person bear all the burden.

00:08:14.703 --> 00:08:16.622
Don't tell me...

00:08:24.922 --> 00:08:26.882
You <i>are </i>still here.

00:08:28.634 --> 00:08:30.177
Sakuraba--

00:08:32.888 --> 00:08:34.389
"Q: You can't say no when someone asks
you to do something." "A: Yes / No / Neither"

00:08:34.389 --> 00:08:39.353
"Q: People often say you are indecisive."
"A: Yes / No / Neither"

00:08:39.353 --> 00:08:48.111
Which am I...? I don't think
I'm that indecisive... No, but...

00:08:48.111 --> 00:08:50.072
Neither, I think?

00:08:50.072 --> 00:08:52.241
She's completely indecisive.

00:08:52.241 --> 00:08:54.701
"Result"
Okay, was that the last question?

00:08:54.701 --> 00:08:56.370
"You are a 'barnacle type.'"

00:08:56.620 --> 00:09:02.709
A barnacle? I'm not a barnacle!
I-I'm taking it again...

00:09:02.709 --> 00:09:03.919
How's this?!

00:09:03.919 --> 00:09:05.462
"You are a 'sea urchin type.'"

00:09:06.964 --> 00:09:08.632
"You are a 'sea star type.'"

00:09:09.216 --> 00:09:10.843
"You are a 'sea anemone type.'"

00:09:11.593 --> 00:09:14.012
Please... at least a fish...

00:09:14.179 --> 00:09:16.473
"You are a 'moray eel type.'"

00:09:16.765 --> 00:09:19.142
Yes! I got a fish-type!

00:09:20.519 --> 00:09:23.480
Did you learn your lesson? Oh, dear...

00:09:24.606 --> 00:09:25.899
Kakei?!

00:09:33.156 --> 00:09:34.199
That was close--

00:09:34.199 --> 00:09:35.492
Hey!

00:09:41.582 --> 00:09:46.295
I wasn't goofing off.
I was looking something up, and...

00:09:46.295 --> 00:09:48.046
It's okay, it makes me feel better.

00:09:48.046 --> 00:09:50.799
I thought you were working
hard even though you were tired.

00:09:50.799 --> 00:09:52.134
Huh?

00:09:57.639 --> 00:10:01.685
I think I should really
be working harder, though.

00:10:01.685 --> 00:10:05.355
You've done enough, you know.
Are you sleeping properly?

00:10:05.355 --> 00:10:11.069
Oh, there's no... problem with that.

00:10:12.321 --> 00:10:14.573
There <i>is </i>a problem, huh?

00:10:14.573 --> 00:10:16.867
Come closer. You'll get wet.

00:10:16.867 --> 00:10:18.619
Uh, right...

00:10:31.298 --> 00:10:35.594
I get uneasy when I'm not working hard.

00:10:35.594 --> 00:10:38.430
You're a hard worker, Sakuraba.

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:41.975
The Library Club runs smoothly because of you.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.687
You should relax more.

00:10:45.687 --> 00:10:49.274
If you're not having fun, then
there's no point in the Happy Project.

00:10:49.274 --> 00:10:52.986
I see. That's true.

00:10:57.491 --> 00:10:59.034
Thanks.

00:11:02.538 --> 00:11:04.831
The rain stopped.

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.962
Sakurab--

00:11:20.013 --> 00:11:24.101
It looks like many things
happened while I was gone.

00:11:25.936 --> 00:11:30.899
Kyotaro Kakei has passed the preliminary exam.

00:11:32.442 --> 00:11:34.987
Stop playing around with the emails.

00:11:34.987 --> 00:11:36.530
You knew?

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:41.034
Your job was just to observe him.

00:11:43.161 --> 00:11:45.622
Am I disqualified?

00:11:45.622 --> 00:11:52.921
No, but as I said before, at this rate, you
won't advance past being a Shepherd candidate.

00:11:56.133 --> 00:12:01.180
There's no point if you don't
realize what you're lacking yourself.

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:03.015
You know that, right?

00:12:07.603 --> 00:12:10.480
What am I doing...?

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:13.108
I want to be the Shepherd, right?

00:12:13.108 --> 00:12:17.613
I can't let him get ahead of me. I just can't.

00:12:26.955 --> 00:12:28.707
What is all that noise?

00:12:28.707 --> 00:12:33.128
Hello! It's your wonderful neighbor, Kodachi!

00:12:33.128 --> 00:12:36.089
You said you saw the real culprit in a dream?

00:12:36.089 --> 00:12:39.176
Is that what you call a prophetic dream?

00:12:39.176 --> 00:12:43.263
Kakei, do you believe in prophetic
dreams or predicting the future?

00:12:43.263 --> 00:12:45.015
What's with the sudden interest?

00:12:45.015 --> 00:12:47.726
It might be kind of hard
if you could see the future, huh?

00:12:47.726 --> 00:12:54.274
It'd be fine if you always saw a bright future,
but it'd probably be hard to see a dark future.

00:12:57.402 --> 00:13:01.114
This happened 'cause that
guy said someone'd get hurt.

00:13:01.114 --> 00:13:03.450
That's rotten.

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:08.914
Kakei, could you possibly
be able to see the future?

00:13:08.914 --> 00:13:11.166
If I said I could, would you believe me?

00:13:11.166 --> 00:13:17.089
My parents also have that kind
of sixth sense, so I probably would.

00:13:17.089 --> 00:13:19.591
I see...

00:13:20.926 --> 00:13:25.556
Actually, I get premonitions sometimes.

00:13:25.556 --> 00:13:29.601
Ever since I was little,
I'd see a vision of a strange library.

00:13:30.853 --> 00:13:34.189
It just kept going and going...

00:13:34.189 --> 00:13:37.818
And there was a magic book there...

00:13:39.194 --> 00:13:42.406
It was filled with letters I couldn't read.

00:13:42.406 --> 00:13:44.700
Whenever I saw someone's future,

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:48.620
most of the time, it was preceded
by a vision of that library.

00:13:49.997 --> 00:13:52.457
Then, look at my future.

00:13:52.457 --> 00:13:53.917
Um...

00:13:53.917 --> 00:13:56.503
Come on, just for a little?

00:13:57.796 --> 00:14:01.258
For the record, it doesn't always work, okay?

00:14:07.139 --> 00:14:08.348
Hey...

00:14:29.745 --> 00:14:31.747
Huh?

00:14:31.747 --> 00:14:33.999
What was that just now...?

00:14:33.999 --> 00:14:35.584
Did you see something?

00:14:35.584 --> 00:14:40.088
There was like an invisible wall,
and I couldn't go past it.

00:14:40.088 --> 00:14:41.924
An invisible wall...

00:14:43.425 --> 00:14:45.385
Man, that's lame!

00:14:45.385 --> 00:14:47.054
Where's the future where
I'm sitting in a bathtub full of money

00:14:47.054 --> 00:14:49.348
with a wine glass in one hand?

00:14:49.348 --> 00:14:51.266
What the heck?

00:14:51.266 --> 00:14:54.978
For some reason, that made
me tired. I'm going home.

00:14:57.606 --> 00:15:00.025
No matter what the result was,
at least you looked at it for me.

00:15:00.025 --> 00:15:03.278
I'll just be glad you didn't see a bad future.

00:15:09.451 --> 00:15:13.372
It was completely blank,
like there was nothing there...

00:15:13.372 --> 00:15:16.041
It was the first time that happened...

00:15:17.167 --> 00:15:19.294
What was that?

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:23.757
He was able to see it.

00:15:23.757 --> 00:15:28.762
Kyotaro Kakei has passed the preliminary exam.

00:15:35.519 --> 00:15:38.480
The Shepherd? What's that?

00:15:38.480 --> 00:15:41.400
Anyway, I don't know anything. Later.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:42.985
Hey, wait!

00:15:42.985 --> 00:15:44.611
It's no use, huh?

00:15:44.611 --> 00:15:47.281
This is the third person.

00:15:47.281 --> 00:15:51.702
They're the ones who
said they saw the Shepherd...

00:15:51.702 --> 00:15:53.871
I wonder why they don't remember?

00:15:53.871 --> 00:15:57.040
And all three of them, too.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:16:00.878
I wonder if our memories can
become completely blank like that?

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:03.130
Blank...

00:16:06.592 --> 00:16:08.177
Kakei?

00:16:08.177 --> 00:16:12.306
Uh... Anyway, we bought a lot, huh?

00:16:12.306 --> 00:16:15.350
There were still some things we needed.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:17.561
And we needed some things for Master Giza, too.

00:16:17.561 --> 00:16:20.105
You've been completely charmed
by Master Giza, haven't you?

00:16:20.105 --> 00:16:22.274
Kanasuke, are you jealous?

00:16:22.274 --> 00:16:24.526
Well, it kind of breaks up our duo.

00:16:24.526 --> 00:16:25.569
Duo?

00:16:25.569 --> 00:16:28.488
Yeah! Our lovely first-year duo--

00:16:28.488 --> 00:16:31.033
"Kanasuke and Misono"!

00:16:31.033 --> 00:16:33.076
Not very original.

00:16:33.535 --> 00:16:36.622
"Kanasuke"... That's nice...

00:16:36.622 --> 00:16:37.623
Misono?

00:16:37.623 --> 00:16:42.503
U-Um... You don't have to be
so formal when speaking to me.

00:16:42.503 --> 00:16:44.338
Then, Misono.

00:16:44.338 --> 00:16:45.964
Then, I'll call you Senri.

00:16:45.964 --> 00:16:47.299
We're on a first-name basis now?

00:16:47.299 --> 00:16:48.592
Well, we <i>are </i>a duo.

00:16:48.592 --> 00:16:50.260
I don't remember forming it with you.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:52.221
We're already about to break up!

00:16:52.221 --> 00:16:53.847
What should I do?

00:16:53.847 --> 00:16:55.933
It's no good coming crying to me.

00:16:56.975 --> 00:16:58.977
Oh, Kana.

00:16:58.977 --> 00:17:02.856
D-Did you just call me "Kana"?

00:17:02.856 --> 00:17:05.776
You're the one that used my first name first.

00:17:05.776 --> 00:17:07.736
That's fine, Senri!

00:17:08.946 --> 00:17:10.781
Say it again!

00:17:14.743 --> 00:17:15.786
That's...

00:17:15.786 --> 00:17:16.745
Kodachi?

00:17:16.745 --> 00:17:18.497
Sorry, you guys go ahead.

00:17:18.497 --> 00:17:20.249
Hey...

00:17:21.208 --> 00:17:22.835
Kakei?

00:17:24.545 --> 00:17:26.088
Kodachi!

00:17:32.928 --> 00:17:36.056
Wait a minute. About last night...

00:17:38.016 --> 00:17:39.601
Nya!

00:17:40.853 --> 00:17:42.354
Hey!

00:17:44.857 --> 00:17:46.900
Last night?

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:48.902
I wonder what happened...

00:17:57.703 --> 00:17:59.413
She's gone...

00:17:59.705 --> 00:18:01.456
"Come on, baby!"

00:18:02.291 --> 00:18:04.251
What the...?

00:18:04.251 --> 00:18:07.421
Those two are definitely suspicious!

00:18:07.421 --> 00:18:11.341
Kakei said something about "last night."

00:18:11.341 --> 00:18:14.261
I wonder if they were together all night again?

00:18:14.261 --> 00:18:16.221
How indecent.

00:18:16.221 --> 00:18:18.807
At night, a man and a woman,

00:18:18.807 --> 00:18:21.143
--alone together in a room...
--No... Don't...

00:18:21.143 --> 00:18:25.480
There had to have been some
scandalous developments, huh?

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:26.440
Most likely.

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:30.527
I-I didn't know they were so close...

00:18:30.527 --> 00:18:32.279
Shirasaki, the tea!

00:18:33.906 --> 00:18:35.824
It's bothering her a lot, huh?

00:18:35.824 --> 00:18:36.992
Yeah.

00:18:36.992 --> 00:18:39.661
Th-That is incorrect!

00:18:39.661 --> 00:18:41.455
No, no, no.

00:18:41.455 --> 00:18:43.665
There's no place for us here.

00:19:06.438 --> 00:19:08.982
What in the world is she...?

00:19:18.659 --> 00:19:19.910
What's up?

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:21.745
Do you have a minute?

00:19:21.745 --> 00:19:23.956
I wanted to ask about your schedule next week.

00:19:23.956 --> 00:19:25.791
Are you free on Tuesday?

00:19:25.791 --> 00:19:29.545
Oh, d-don't misunderstand.
I'm not asking you on a date.

00:19:29.545 --> 00:19:32.673
This is just... Wait, what am I--?

00:19:32.673 --> 00:19:34.842
Hey, you're still here?

00:19:34.842 --> 00:19:37.761
Kodachi, sorry. I was about to leave.

00:19:37.761 --> 00:19:39.471
Kodachi?

00:19:40.472 --> 00:19:41.390
Kakei?

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:44.935
Oh, yeah. I'm free Tuesday.

00:19:44.935 --> 00:19:48.188
I can move things or clean or whatever.

00:19:48.188 --> 00:19:50.440
Great, thanks.

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:52.901
It's raining. Do you have an umbrella?

00:19:52.901 --> 00:19:55.654
Yeah, I have one today.

00:19:55.654 --> 00:19:58.198
Oh good, then hurry up and go home.

00:19:58.198 --> 00:20:00.534
Yeah, thanks.

00:20:05.247 --> 00:20:06.582
Hm?

00:20:09.918 --> 00:20:10.961
Shut up!

00:20:10.961 --> 00:20:13.839
--Do you know what time it is?
--Kodachi? Why...

00:20:18.635 --> 00:20:21.638
Hey, what's going on?

00:20:32.107 --> 00:20:35.777
It's a lie that you live here, isn't it?

00:20:37.362 --> 00:20:41.742
Shirasaki and the others
didn't remember you, either...

00:20:44.119 --> 00:20:45.662
"To: The Shepherd"
"What do I have to do to meet you?"

00:20:46.705 --> 00:20:49.458
Kodachi...

00:20:49.458 --> 00:20:52.127
Are you the Shepherd?

00:20:53.086 --> 00:20:55.631
This is how it ends, huh?

00:20:55.631 --> 00:21:00.886
Yeah, I'm the Shepherd who sent those emails.

00:21:05.098 --> 00:21:06.683
Congratulations.

00:21:09.311 --> 00:21:13.899
You've passed the
preliminary exam, Kyotaro Kakei.

00:21:21.615 --> 00:21:25.452
I'm celebrating for you.

00:21:26.203 --> 00:21:28.330
Now, shall we go?

00:21:29.706 --> 00:21:33.168
To the magic library.

00:21:33.168 --> 00:21:36.004
The magic library...?

00:21:50.435 --> 00:21:59.194
<i>The starting bell, the sound of a lock</i>

00:21:59.194 --> 00:22:06.869
<i>While drifting aimlessly, I become an adult</i>

00:22:06.869 --> 00:22:16.712
<i>The time has come when days spent</i>
<i>running and playing seem far away</i>

00:22:16.712 --> 00:22:20.966
<i>The answer I gave here</i>

00:22:20.966 --> 00:22:33.896
<i>Oh, if only it had been</i>
<i>passed down somewhere</i>

00:22:33.896 --> 00:22:38.692
<i>For those crowds walking around lost</i>

00:22:38.692 --> 00:22:43.030
<i>It can be a light that shines on them</i>

00:22:43.030 --> 00:22:51.330
<i>On the other side of the</i>
<i>green belt that surrounds us</i>

00:22:51.330 --> 00:22:59.713
<i>You head toward endless tomorrows</i>

00:23:11.558 --> 00:23:14.603
Man, why do I have to celebrate for Kakei?

00:23:14.603 --> 00:23:16.313
The boss is so mean...

00:23:16.313 --> 00:23:20.400
Fine. If he wants me to celebrate so bad,
then I'll give him something special!

00:23:20.400 --> 00:23:25.155
Ta-da! Koda's special
"Kakei-should-just-be-blown-away" Deluxe!

00:23:25.155 --> 00:23:27.741
I'll make him regret making me angry!

00:23:27.741 --> 00:23:29.076
Go, Koda!

00:23:31.036 --> 00:23:33.747
"Next time: The Magic Library"
Shooting star...

00:23:33.747 --> 00:23:37.131
"Next time: The Magic Library"
